Q: What does &quot;std:&quot; mean? (with one colon) A: <p>It is parsed as a <a href="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/goto.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer">goto label</a>. Unfortunately it is still part of C++ language, even though it is <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/3517726/what-is-wrong-with-using-goto">widely hated</a> by engineers.</p>
<pre><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;

using namespace std;

int main() {
    std:
        cerr &lt;&lt; &quot;5&quot;;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Technically you could use <code>goto std;</code> to jump to it. Now if you remove <code>using namespace std;</code> the symbol <code>cerr</code> is unknown.</p>

Q: I can&#39;t smooth out the rounded bottom corners of an HTML table with CSS A: <p>You're adding <code>border-radius</code> to too many elements, they're overlapping each other and it's leading to the 'ghosting' effect you're observing. You also need to use <code>separate</code> border collapse to get <code>border-radius</code> to work on tables, but that comes with it's own problems.</p>
<p>Instead of focusing on adding <code>border-radius</code> to the individual rows/elements, utilize the <code>.table-wrapper</code> div instead:</p>
<pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.table-wrapper {
    position: initial;
    width: 100% !important;
    max-width: 100% !important;
    overflow-x: auto !important;
    box-shadow: none !important;
    margin-top: 28px !important;
    margin-bottom: 28px !important;
    background-color: transparent !important;
    display: block !important;
    /* add the radius and border here, instead: */
    border-radius: 8px !important;
    border: 1px solid #b3b5ba /* your color here */;

    table {
        border-collapse: collapse;
        box-sizing: border-box !important;
        line-height: 1.4rem !important;
        /* remove this: 
        border-radius: 10px !important; */

        thead {
            box-sizing: border-box !important;
            color: #494c54;
            font-size: 18px !important;

            /* remove this:
            tr {
                border-radius: 8px !important;
            }
            */

            tr th {
                box-sizing: border-box !important;
                border-collapse: collapse !important;
                background-color: #e1e2e5d4;
                height: 1.5rem !important;
                border-right: 1px solid #c0c0c0 !important;
                border-bottom: 1px solid #d1d1d1 !important;
                &amp;:last-of-type {
                    border-right: none !important;
                }
            }
        }
        tbody {
            tr td {
                box-sizing: border-box !important;
                border-bottom: 1px solid #a8abb0 !important;
                border-right: 1px solid #a8abb087 !important;
            }
            tr:last-of-type td {
                /* no border for the bottom cells: */
                border-bottom: none !important;
            }
            tr td:last-of-type {
                /* no border for the rightmost cells: */
                border-right: none !important;
            }
        }
    }
}

@media (min-width: 31.25rem) {
    tr,
    td {
        font-size: .875rem !important;
    }
    th {
        font-size: .961rem !important;
        font-family: &quot;Helvetica Now Text&quot; !important;
    }
}
</code></pre>
